1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:09,930
September 14, 1968. Five university workers from Puebla set out to climb the volcano La Malinche. They only needed somewhere to sleep.

2
00:00:09,950 --> 00:00:18,810
Heavy rain and nightfall forced them to stop in the village of San Miguel Canoa. A local man, Lucas García, offered them shelter in his home.

3
00:00:18,830 --> 00:00:24,490
But in Canoa, the parish priest had been preaching fear. Communists, he warned, were coming.

4
00:00:24,510 --> 00:00:32,200
That night, the church bells rang. Voices shouted that the communists had arrived… that they had come to kill, and to steal the women.

5
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:35,250
Nearly eight hundred people surrounded the house.

6
00:00:35,270 --> 00:00:45,660
Two of the visitors, Jesús Carrillo and Ramón Gutiérrez, were killed. So was Lucas, the man who took them in. Four people died. The three survivors were gravely injured.

7
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:50,070
They were not agitators. They were hikers, looking for a place to sleep.

8
00:00:50,090 --> 00:01:00,632
The priest accused of inciting the crowd was never convicted. There was no ghost in Canoa. Only a rumor… and a crowd that believed it. This is Plot Twist with A&R.

